  m_Name: AnkylosaurusData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AnimalData
  animalName: Ankylosaurus
  scientificName: Ankylosaurus magniventris
  classification: Armored Herbivore (Plant Eater)
  era: Late Cretaceous (~68 - 66 Million Years Ago)
  averageLength: 8.0 meters (26 ft)
  averageWeight: 6,000 kg (6 metric tons)
  description: 'Ankylosaurus was a heavily armored herbivore that coexisted alongside
    Tyrannosaurus Rex, acting as the living tank of the Late Cretaceous ecosystem.
    Measuring roughly 25 to 30 feet in length, its low-slung, broad body was covered
    from head to tail in a fortress of thick osteoderms, bony plates, and fused armor
    embedded directly into its skin. Even its eyelids were protected by bony plates,
    leaving almost no vulnerable soft tissue exposed to attacking predators. If a
    carnivore attempted an ambush, Ankylosaurus could hunker down to protect its
    unarmored underbelly and swing its signature defense weapon: a massive, heavy
    tail club formed from fused vertebrae and solid bone. A single powerful blow
    from this club was fully capable of shattering the legs or ribs of any pursuing
    predator.'
  funFact: Ankylosaurus wielded a massive club of solid bone at the end of its tail,
    powerful enough to break the leg bones of an attacking T-Rex!
